/C [ 0 0 0 ] /Contents (Define refinance as financing supplied to a lender against eligible loans it has made. HFC means housing finance company. A primary lending institution, or PLI, deals with the household. NHB works mainly through this institutional layer. The distinction matters because NHB refinance eligibility and household loan approval are different decisions. Source detail: Annual Report 2025\20526, printed pp.20 and 32\20534. The FAQ contains old ownership and regulation wording. Only its statement on the absence of direct individual loans is used here.) /QuadPoints [ 1245 686 1260 686 1245 701 1260 701 ] /Rect [ 1245 686 1260 701 ] /Subtype /Text /Type /Annot
>>
endobj
